# Project Structure

```
serverless.ts            # Serverless Framework: single HTTP API Gateway
services/products/       # NestJS Lambda — /products/**
services/customers/      # NestJS Lambda — /customers/**
services/deliveries/     # NestJS Lambda — /deliveries/**
services/transactions/   # NestJS Lambda — /transactions/**
apps/web/                # React SPA + Redux (S3/CloudFront via Serverless later)
packages/persistence/    # ElectroDB entities, repository adapters, seed (`@app/persistence`)
packages/shared/         # logger, access-log middleware, security headers, types
```

Each Nest service exposes `src/lambda.ts` for the root `serverless.ts` HTTP API. Do not add a custom gateway Node service.

## Naming

- Product/app name: neutral store brand; never the payment company name.
- Packages: `@app/shared`, `@app/web`, `@app/products`, etc. — not provider-prefixed.
- Commits: feature-focused; never mention the forbidden brand.

## Implementation order (when coding starts)

Follow `specs/checkout-payment/tasks.md` (T0→T9). Summary:

1. `packages/shared` logger + security headers (T0)  
2. DynamoDB + ElectroDB + seed (T1)  
3. Nest use-cases + ports (ROP) + Jest (T2–T4)  
4. HTTP adapters + OpenAPI/Apidog (T5)  
5. FE screens + Redux persist (T6–T7)  
6. Coverage + `serverless deploy` + README (T8–T9)  

Do not skip tests — coverage is the highest single score item.
